WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.919
Hi, I'm Nova!

00:00:02.919 --> 00:00:06.546
Most video generators paint pictures, then guess the 3D.

00:00:06.546 --> 00:00:08.965
GAE generates where geometry already lives.

00:00:08.965 --> 00:00:09.771
Here's how.

00:00:11.558 --> 00:00:14.677
Generate in a latent a geometry model already reads.

00:00:14.677 --> 00:00:18.143
Decode the picture and the 3D from that same state.

00:00:18.143 --> 00:00:20.223
The geometry never sees the picture.

00:00:21.758 --> 00:00:23.866
Start with Depth Anything 3, frozen.

00:00:23.866 --> 00:00:27.028
It reads frames into four levels of rich features.

00:00:27.448 --> 00:00:31.349
A codec squeezes those into sixty-four channels on the same patch grid.

00:00:31.349 --> 00:00:33.624
Only the channels shrink, never the grid.

00:00:34.044 --> 00:00:37.765
Then a flow model generates in that space: from noise, guided by

00:00:37.765 --> 00:00:41.176
a reference image and camera rays, to a latent per view.

00:00:42.925 --> 00:00:43.715
Why compress?

00:00:43.715 --> 00:00:44.110
Conditioning.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:48.851
The raw features' condition number is six point six times ten to

00:00:48.851 --> 00:00:50.432
the sixteenth: numerically singular.

00:00:50.432 --> 00:00:52.012
The latent's is fifty-three.

00:00:53.883 --> 00:00:56.682
To read a latent out, a shared trunk decodes it once.

00:00:57.102 --> 00:01:01.092
One fork is a learned RGB head, two hundred and three million

00:01:01.092 --> 00:01:02.755
parameters, that paints the pixels.

00:01:03.175 --> 00:01:07.377
The other rebuilds four feature levels for Depth Anything's frozen head, which

00:01:07.377 --> 00:01:09.129
reads depth and camera rays.

00:01:09.549 --> 00:01:12.226
No path runs from the pixels to the geometry.

00:01:12.226 --> 00:01:15.795
Delete the RGB head and you'd get the same cloud, in grey.

00:01:17.317 --> 00:01:19.817
Each point is built from the geometry readout alone.

00:01:20.237 --> 00:01:23.025
Origin: the camera centre, from the decoded ray.

00:01:23.478 --> 00:01:25.128
Plus depth, from the frozen head,

00:01:26.524 --> 00:01:27.855
times the ray's direction.

00:01:27.855 --> 00:01:30.186
The picture only sets each point's colour.

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:33.444
Geometry is read, not reconstructed.

00:01:33.444 --> 00:01:38.726
Picture and 3D fork from one latent, and the points never touch the pixels.

00:01:40.192 --> 00:01:45.011
To recap: generate where geometry lives, fork two readouts, and build points from rays.

00:01:45.431 --> 00:01:47.488
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:47.488 --> 00:01:48.076
I'm Nova.

00:01:48.076 --> 00:01:48.370
Bye!
